---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Ember from "../components/Ember.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Kindling | Start the task you are avoiding"
  description="Kindling helps you start the one thing you are avoiding with a tiny first step and a short timer."
>
  <section class="hero section-shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">A gentle task starter for iPhone</p>
      <h1>Kindling helps you start the one thing you are avoiding.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lede">
        Name the task. Get one small, concrete first step. Start a two or five minute timer and let that be enough for now.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="#how-it-works">
          See how it works <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href="/support/">Get support</a>
      </div>
      <ul class="trust-list" aria-label="Kindling principles">
        <li>No account</li>
        <li>Works offline</li>
        <li>No streaks</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-visual">
      <div class="hearth hearth--outer" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hearth hearth--inner" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <Ember variant="hero" sparks />
      <div class="mini-session" aria-label="Example Kindling session">
        <span>First step</span>
        <strong>Open the document.</strong>
        <span class="mini-timer">02:00</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="manifesto">
    <div class="section-shell manifesto-inner">
      <p data-reveal>
        You already know what needs doing. Kindling makes the distance to <strong>starting</strong> smaller.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="loop section-shell" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="loop-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">One calm loop</p>
      <h2 id="loop-title">From stuck to started.</h2>
      <p>No planning system to maintain. Just three small moves that help you begin what is in front of you.</p>
    </div>

    <ol class="beats">
      <li data-reveal>
        <span class="beat-number">01</span>
        <div class="flow-preview flow-preview--entry" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>What are you avoiding?</span>
          <strong>Book the appointment</strong>
        </div>
        <h3>Enter one task</h3>
        <p>Write it in your own words. You do not need to sort the rest of your day first.</p>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span class="beat-number">02</span>
        <div class="flow-preview flow-preview--step" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Your first step</span>
          <strong>Open your calendar.</strong>
        </div>
        <h3>Receive a tiny first step</h3>
        <p>Kindling suggests one concrete action. Local templates always work, even without a connection.</p>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal>
        <span class="beat-number">03</span>
        <div class="flow-preview flow-preview--timer" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Stay with this step</span>
          <strong>02:00</strong>
        </div>
        <h3>Start a short timer</h3>
        <p>Choose two or five minutes. Keep going, stop for now, or notice a distraction without judgment.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-section">
    <div class="section-shell feature-grid">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Built for the moment</p>
        <h2>Support that stays out of the way.</h2>
        <p>
          A Live Activity can keep the countdown visible on your Lock Screen or Dynamic Island. Optional notifications can let you know when the timer ends without showing your task title.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="privacy-card" data-reveal>
        <img src="/assets/kindling-app-icon.webp" alt="Kindling app icon" width="256" height="256" decoding="async" />
        <div>
          <h3>Local by default</h3>
          <p>Your tasks are stored on your iPhone. Kindling has no account, and offline first steps are always available.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy policy</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="plus section-shell" id="kindling-plus" aria-labelledby="plus-title">
    <div class="plus-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Kindling Plus</p>
      <h2 id="plus-title">Keep more than one task warm.</h2>
      <p>
        The complete rescue flow is free for one active task at a time. Kindling Plus lets you park and return to multiple tasks.
      </p>
      <p class="fine-print">
        Plus is offered in the app through Apple as monthly and annual subscriptions and as a non-expiring, one-time Kindling Plus Lifetime purchase. The App Store purchase screen shows current localized prices and trial eligibility before you confirm. <a href="/terms/#plus">See what Lifetime means</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="task-stack" aria-label="Example of multiple parked tasks" data-reveal>
      <article><span>Ready</span><strong>Send the application</strong><small>Open the draft.</small></article>
      <article><span>Parked</span><strong>Sort the paperwork</strong><small>Put one envelope on the table.</small></article>
      <article><span>Parked</span><strong>Reply to Sam</strong><small>Open the conversation.</small></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="not-section">
    <div class="section-shell not-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Deliberately focused</p>
        <h2>Less pressure. Less planning.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="not-list">
        <article data-reveal>
          <span aria-hidden="true">1</span>
          <div><h3>Not a day planner</h3><p>Kindling helps with the task in front of you, not an entire schedule.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article data-reveal>
          <span aria-hidden="true">2</span>
          <div><h3>Not a streak</h3><p>No missed day warning, score, or mascot disappointment. Coming back is enough.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article data-reveal>
          <span aria-hidden="true">3</span>
          <div><h3>Not medical care</h3><p>Kindling is a productivity tool. It does not diagnose, treat, or provide crisis support.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quote-section section-shell" aria-label="Kindling principle">
    <Ember variant="inline" />
    <blockquote data-reveal>Starting small still counts as starting.</blockquote>
    <a class="button button--secondary" href="/support/">Questions? Visit support</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
